# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Fridrich Apartman frontend project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File**: `package.json`
- **Change**: Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version `^2.0.0` to dependencies
- **Package Manager**: pnpm (as specified in package.json)

### 2. Speed Insights Integration
- **File**: `src/App.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Imported `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the App component, positioned alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component

### 3. Lock File Update
- **File**: `pnpm-lock.yaml`
- **Change**: Updated with new dependency resolution for @vercel/speed-insights and its peer dependencies

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- **Project Type**: Vite + React (React 18.3.1)
- **Package Manager**: pnpm@8.10.0
- **Documentation Source**: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

### Integration Approach
Following the official Vercel documentation for React applications, the SpeedInsights component was:
1. Imported from the React-specific entry point (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`)
2. Placed in the root App component to ensure it runs on all pages
3. Positioned alongside the existing Analytics component for consistency

### Code Structure Preservation
- Maintained existing code structure and formatting
- Preserved all existing imports and dependencies
- Added Speed Insights component in a logical location (next to Analytics component)
- No breaking changes to existing functionality

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Build Verification**: Build completed successfully without errors
- Command: `pnpm run build`
- Result: Built successfully in 4.30s with optimized chunks

✅ **Linting**: No linting errors introduced
- Command: `pnpm run lint`
- Result: Clean exit with no errors

✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file properly updated
- pnpm-lock.yaml reflects the new @vercel/speed-insights@2.0.0 dependency

## Next Steps for User

1. **Enable Speed Insights on Vercel Dashboard**:
   - Navigate to your Vercel project dashboard
   - Select "Speed Insights" from the sidebar
   - Click "Enable" for this project

2. **Deploy to Vercel**:
   - Push these changes to your Git repository
   - Vercel will automatically deploy the updated application
   - Speed Insights will start collecting data after deployment

3. **View Performance Data**:
   - After deployment and user visits, access Speed Insights in your Vercel dashboard
   - Monitor real-world performance metrics including:
     - Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
     - Time to First Byte (TTFB)
     - First Contentful Paint (FCP)

## Additional Notes

- The Speed Insights component is lightweight and designed for production use
- It automatically collects Web Vitals data from real user sessions
- Works seamlessly alongside the existing @vercel/analytics integration
- No additional configuration required - works out of the box after deployment
